"hadiths[127]{hadithnumber,text}:"
682,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""On the first night of the month of Ramadan"
683,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan and stands (in the night prayer) for it out of faith and seeking a reward (from Allah)"
684,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Do not precede the month with a day nor with two days"
685,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Do no precede the month of Ramadan by fasting a day or two before it"
686,"Silah bin Zufar said:""We were with Ammar bin Yasir when a roasted sheep was brought and he said: 'Eat.' Someone among the people said: 'I am fasting.' So Ammar said: 'Whoever fasts on a day in which there is doubt"
687,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Count the (the appearances of) the crescent of Sha'ban for Ramadan"
688,"Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast with its sighting"
689,"Ibn Mas`ud said:""What I fasted with the Prophet that was twenty-nine (days)"
690,"Anas narrated:""The Messenger of Allah vowed to stay away from his wives for a month"
691,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""A Bedouin came to the Prophet and said: 'I have seen the crescent.' So he said: 'Do you testify that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah? Do you testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' So he said: 'O Bilal! Announce to the people that they should fast tomorrow"
692,"Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah narrated from his father that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""The two months of Eid will not both be deficient: Ramadn and Dhul-Hijjah"
693,"Muhammad bin Abi Harmalah narrated:""Kuraib informed me that Umm Al-Fadl bin Al-Harith sent him to Mu'awiyah in Ash-Sham. He said: 'So I arrived in Ash-Sham and finished her errand"
694,"Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever has dried dates"
695,"Salman bin Amir Ad-Dabbi narrated that :the Prophet said: ""When one of you breaks his fast"
696,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would break the fast with fresh dates before performing Salat. If there were no fresh dates then (he would break the fast) with dried dates"
697,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""The fast is the day the people fast"
698,"Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When the night advances and the day retreats"
699,"Sahl bin Sa'd narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""The people will remain upon goodness as long as they hasten to break the fast"
700,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Allah"
701,"Abu Hurairah narrated:(A Hadith similar to no. 700 with a different chain)"
702,"Abu Atiyyah said:""Masruq and I entered upon Aishah and we said: 'O Mother of the Believers! There are two men from the Companions of Muhammad"
703,"Anas (bin Malik) narrated that :Zaid bin Thabit said: ""We ate Sahar with the Messenger of Allah"
704,"Anas (bin Malik) narrated:(Another chain) except that he said: ""About the length for reciting fifty Ayahs"
705,"Talq bin Ali narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Eat and drink"
706,"Samurah bin Jundub narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Do not let the Adhan of Bilal prevent you from your Sahar"
707,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever does not leave false speech"
708,"Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Partake of Sahar"
709,"Amr bin Al-As narrated :(similar to no. 708) from the Prophet"
710,"Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah went to Makkah in the Year of the Conquest"
711,"Aishah narrated that :Hamzah bin Amr Al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah about fasting while traveling"
712,"Abu Sa'eed (Al-Khudri) narrated:""We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah during the month of Ramadan. No one objected to the fast of the one fasting nor the fast breaking of the one who broke his fast"
713,"Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:""We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah. Some of us were fasting and some of us broke their fast. The one who broke their fast had no objection to the one who fasted"
714,"Ma'mar bin Abi Huyaiyah narrated that:he asked Ibn Al-Musaiyab about fasting on a journey"
715,"# Hadith of Anas ibn Malik al-Kaʿbi رضي الله عنه

**Narrated by Abū Kurayb and Yūsuf ibn ʿĪsā — both of them said:** Wakiʿ narrated to us: Abū Hilāl narrated to us: from ʿAbdullāh ibn Sawādah: from Anas ibn Mālik, a man from the Banī ʿAbdullāh ibn Kaʿb, who said:

""The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم raided us, so I came to the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم and found him taking his lunch. He said, **'Come closer and eat.'** I replied, **'I am fasting.'** He said, **'Come closer, and I will inform you about fasting — or about ṣiyām. Indeed, Allah, the Most High, has exempted the traveller from fasting and from half of the prayer, and has exempted the pregnant woman or the nursing woman from fasting — or from ṣiyām.'**

By Allah, the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم indeed stated both of these — or one of them. Oh, what regret I feel that I did not partake of the food of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم!""

---

**Commentary of Imām Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī رحمه الله:**

Abū ʿĪsā said: ""The hadith of Anas ibn Mālik al-Kaʿbi is a *ḥasan* hadith. We know of no other hadith from this Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم besides this single narration. The established practice (*al-ʿamal*) among the scholars is upon this hadith.""

**Scholarly Opinions on the Pregnant and Nursing Woman:**

Some scholars among the people of knowledge stated: **""The pregnant woman and the nursing woman break their fast, make up the missed fasts, and offer expiatory feeding (*ṭaʿām*).""** This is the position of **Sufyān al-Thawrī, Mālik ibn Anas, al-Shāfiʿī, and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal** رحمه الله.

Others among them stated: **""They break their fast and offer expiatory feeding, but there is no obligation of making up the fasts upon them. However, if they wish to make them up, there is no feeding required of them.""** This is the position of **Isḥāq ibn Rāhwayh** رحمه الله."
716,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""A woman came to the Prophet and said: 'My sister died while she had two consecutive months of fasting due.' So he said: 'Do you not see that if there was a debt due from your sister then you would have to pay it?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then the right of Allah is more appropriate"
717,"Ibn Abbas narrated:(A Hadith similar to no. 716 with a different chain)"
718,"Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever died while he had a month to fast"
719,"Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: ""Three things do not break the fast of the fasting person: Cupping"
720,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever is overcome by vomiting"
721,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever eats or drinks forgetfully"
722,"Abu Hurairah narrated:(Another chain) with the same or similar (Hadith as no)"
723,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever breaks the fast during Ramadan without an allowance or illness"
724,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: A man came to him [the Prophet ﷺ] and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I am destroyed!"" He said: ""What has destroyed you?"" He said: ""I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan."" He said: ""Can you free a slave?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Can you fast two consecutive months?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Can you feed sixty poor people?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Sit down."" So he sat down, and a container full of dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ - and the 'Araq is a large basket - He said: ""Give it in charity."" He said: ""There is no one between its two sides [i.e., the two lava plains of Madinah] poorer than us."" So the Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then said: ""Take it and feed it to your family.""

[Abu 'Eisa said:] There are also narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Umar, 'Aishah, and 'Abdullah bin 'Amr.

Abu 'Eisa said: The Hadith of Abu Hurairah is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. The people of knowledge act upon this Hadith regarding one who breaks the fast in Ramadan intentionally through sexual intercourse. As for one who breaks the fast intentionally through eating or drinking, the people of knowledge have differed about that. Some of them said: He"
725,"Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi'ah narrated from his father who said:""I saw the Prophet - (a number of times) such that I was not able to count - using the Siwak while he was fasting"
726,"Anas bin Malik narrated that :a man came to the Prophet and said: ""My eyes are bothering me"
727,"Aishah narrated:""The Prophet would kiss during the month of fasting"
728,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would fondle me while he was fasting"
729,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would kiss and fondle while he was fasting"
730,"Hafsah narrated that:the Prophet said: ""Whoever did not decide to fast before Fajr then there is no fast for him"
731,"Umm Hani narrated:""I was sitting with the Prophet when some drink was brought"
732,"Simak bin Harb narrated:""A person from the offspring of Umm Hani narrated to me - I met one of the most virtuous among them"
733,"Narrated to us Hanadd, narrated to us Wakee', from Talhah ibn Yahya, from his aunt, 'A'ishah bint Talhah, from 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me one day and said, ""Do you have anything [to eat]?"" She said, ""I said, 'No.' He said, 'Then I am fasting.'"""
734,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by ʿĀʾishah, Umm al-Muʾminīn (may Allāh be pleased with her):**

She said: ""The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) would come to me and say: **'Do you have any food (for the midday meal)?'** I would say: **'No.'** He would then say: **'Then I shall fast.'** She said: ""Then he came to me one day, and I said: **'O Messenger of Allāh, a gift has been presented to us.'** He asked: **'What is it?'** I said: **'Ḥays** (a dish made of dates, clarified butter, and dried yoghurt/curd).' He said: **'Indeed, I have begun the day as one fasting.'** She said: **""Then he ate.""**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""This is a ḥasan (good) hadith.""**

---

## Notes:

- **Ḥays (حَيْس):** A traditional Arabian dish prepared from dates mixed with clarified butter (samn) and dried curd or yoghurt, often considered a delicacy.
- The hadith illustrates the Prophet's (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) graciousness in accepting hospitality and his flexibility regarding voluntary fasting — that one who has intended a voluntary fast may break it if a valid reason arises, such as honouring a gift of food offered by one's host.
- The grading of **ḥasan** was given by Imām al-Tirmidhī (raḥimahullāh)."
735,"Aishah narrated:""Hafsah and I were both fasting when we were presented some food that we really wanted"
736,"Umm Salamah narrated:""I did not see the Prophet fasting two consecutive months except for Sha'ban and Ramadan"
737,"# Scholarly Translation of the Hadith

It was narrated to us Hanād, who narrated from ʿAbdah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, who narrated from Abū Salamah, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding that matter.

It has been narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak that he said regarding this hadith: ""It is permissible in the speech of the Arabs that if a person fasts the majority of the month, it may be said that he fasted the entire month. Likewise, it may be said of a person, 'He stood in prayer the whole night,' even though he may have taken supper or occupied himself with some of his affairs."" It is as though Ibn al-Mubārak regarded both hadiths as being in agreement, saying: ""The meaning of this hadith is simply that he (peace and blessings be upon him) used to fast the majority of the month.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""And Sālim Abū al-Naḍr and others besides him narrated this hadith from Abū Salamah, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), in a manner similar to the narration of Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr."""
738,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""When a half of Sha'ban remains then do not fast"
739,"Aishah narrated:""I could not find the Messenger of Allah one night. So I left and found him at Al-Baqi. He said: 'Did you fear that you had been wronged by Allah and His Messenger?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I thought that you had gone to one of your wives.' So he said: 'Indeed Allah"
740,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""The most virtuous fasting after the month of Ramadan is Allah's month Al-Muharram"
741,"An-Nu'man bin Sa'd narrated:""A man asked Ali: ""Which month do you order me to fast after the month of Ramadan?' He said to him"
742,"Abdullah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would fasting during the beginning of every month for three days"
743,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts before it"
744,"Abdullah bin Busr narrated from his sister that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Do not fast on Saturday except for what has been made obligatory upon you (by Allah). If one of you does not find but a grape peal or a tree's twig"
745,"Aishah narrated:""The Prophet used to try to fast on Mondays and Thursdays"
746,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would fast Saturdays, Sundays, and Mondays in one months, and Tuesdays, Wednesdays and Thursdays in the next month."""
747,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: ""Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday"
748,"Ubaidullah (bin Muslim) Al-Qurashi narrated from his father who said:""I asked - or; the Prophet was asked - about fasting daily. So he said: 'Your family has a right over you.' Then he said: 'Fast Ramadan and that which is after it"
749,"Abu Qatadah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Fast the Day of Arafah"
750,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', who narrated from Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah, who narrated from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) broke his fast at 'Arafah, and Umm al-Fadl sent milk to him, so he drank it.**

**In this chapter, there are narrations from Abu Hurayrah, Ibn 'Umar, and Umm al-Fadl (may Allah be pleased with them all).**

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** The hadith of Ibn 'Abbas is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith.

**It has also been narrated from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said:** ""I performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he did not fast on that day — meaning the Day of 'Arafah. And I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr, and he did not fast it. And with 'Umar, and he did not fast it. And with 'Uthman, and he did not fast it.""

**Abu 'Isa said:** The practice (*al-'amal*) according to the majority of the scholars is that they recommend breaking the fast (*al-iftar*) at 'Arafah, so that a person may thereby gain strength for supplication (*du'aa'*). However, some of the scholars did fast on the Day of 'Arafah while at 'Arafah."
751,"Ibn Abi Najib narrated from his father who said:""Ibn Umar was asked about fasting (the Day of) Arafah (at Arafat). He said: 'I performed Hajj with the Prophet"
752,"Abu Qatadah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Fast the Day of Ashura"
753,"Aishah narrated:""Ashura was a day that the Quraish used to fast during Jahiliyyah"
754,"Al-Hakam bin Al-Arfaj said:""I met up with Ibn Abbas while he was reclining on his Rida at the Zamzam (well). So I said: 'Inform me about the Day of Ashura. On which day is it fasted?' He said: 'When you see the crescent of Al-Muharram"
755,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Messenger of Allah ordered fasting the tenth day for the Day of Ashura"
756,"Aishah narrated:""I did not see the Prophet fasting at all during the ten"
757,"Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah than those ten days."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Not even Jihad in Allah Cause?"" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Not even Jihad in Allah's Cause"
758,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""There are no days more beloved to Allah that He be worshipped in them than the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah"
759,"Narrated Abu Ayyub: that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it with six days of Shawwal, that is (equivalent to) fasting the entire year.""

There are also narrations on this topic from Jabir, Abu Hurairah, and Thawban.

[Abu 'Eisa said:] The Hadith of Abu Ayyub is Hasan Sahih. Some people have recommended fasting six days of Shawwal on the basis of this Hadith. Ibn Al-Mubarak said: ""It is Hasan; it is similar to fasting three days from every month."" Ibn Al-Mubarak said: ""It is reported in some of the Hadith: 'And this fast is joined to Ramadan.'"" Ibn Al-Mubarak preferred that the six days be at the beginning of the month. It has been reported from Ibn Al-Mubarak that he said: ""If one fasts six days of Shawwal separately (not consecutively), then that is permissible.""

He said: 'Abdul-Aziz bin Muhammad reported this from Safwan bin Sulaim and Sa'd bin Sa'eed, from 'Umar bin Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (ﷺ). Shu'bah reported this Hadith from Warqa' bin 'Umar, from Sa'd bin Sa'eed. Sa'd bin Sa'eed is the brother of Yahya bin Sa'eed Al-Ansari, and some of the people of Hadith have criticized Sa'd bin Sa'eed with regard to his memory.

Narrated Al-Hasan Al-Basri: that when the fasting of six days of Shawwal was mentioned in his presence, he would say: ""By Allah, indeed Allah has been pleased to make the fasting of this month equivalent to the fasting of the whole year."""
760,"Abu Hurairah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah took a covenant from me for three: To not sleep except after performing Witr"
761,"Abu Dharr narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""O Abu Dharr! When you fast three days out of a month"
762,"Abu Dharr narrated:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever fasts three days in every month"
763,"Yazid Ar-Rishk said:""I heard Mu'adhah saying to Aishah: 'Did the Messenger of Allah fast three days of every month?' She replied in the affirmative. So she said: 'Which of them would he fast?' She said: 'Which of them he would fast was not noticeable"
764,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed your Lord said: 'Every good deed is rewarded with ten of the same up to seven hundred times over. Fasting is for Me"
765,"Sahl bin Sa'd narrated that:The Prophet said: ""There is a gate in Paradise called Ar-Raiyyan"
766,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There are two joys for the fasting person: the joy when he breaks his fast"
767,"Abu Qatadah said:""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is the case of the one who fasts daily?' He said: 'He did not fast nor break (the fast).'"" Or"
768,"Abdullah bin Shaqiq narrated:""I asked Aishah about the Prophet's fasting.' She said: 'He would fast until we said: ""He has fasted"" and he would abstain from fasting until we said: ""He has abstained from fasting."" (She said:) 'The Messenger of Allah did not fast an entire month except Ramadan"
769,"Jafar bin Humaid narrated that:Anas bin Malik was asked about the Prophet's fasting and he said: ""He would fast during a month until we thought that he did not want to abstain from fasting during any of it. And"
770,"Abdullah bin Amr narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The most virtuous fast is the fast of my brother Dawud. He would fast a day"
771,"Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Shawārib narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū ʿUbayd, the freedman of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said: I witnessed ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr) begin with the prayer before the sermon. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibit fasting on these two days. As for the Day of Breaking Fast (Yawm al-Fiṭr), it is your breaking of your fast and a festival for the Muslims; and as for the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Aḍḥā), then eat from the meat of your sacrifices.

This is a ṣaḥīḥ hadith. Abū ʿUbayd, the freedman of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, whose name is Saʿd, is also referred to as the freedman of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Azhar. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Azhar is the paternal cousin of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf."
772,"Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:""The Messenger of Allah prohibited two fasts: Fasting the Day of Adha and the Day of Fitr"
773,"Uqbah bin Amir narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""The Day of Arafah"
774,"Muhammad bin Yahya, Muhammad bin Rafi' An-Naisaburi, Mahmud bin Ghailan, and Yahya bin Musa narrated to us, they said: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya bin Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qarith, from As-Sa'ib bin Yazid, from Rafi' bin Khadij, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: ""The one who performs cupping and the one who has cupping performed on him have both broken their fast.""

Abu Eisa said: There are narrations on this topic from Ali, Sa'd, Shaddad bin Aws, Thawban, Usamah bin Zaid, Aishah, Ma'qil bin Sinan - and it is also said Ibn Yasar - Abu Hurairah, Ibn Abbas, Abu Musa, and Bilal.

Abu Eisa said: The Hadith of Rafi' bin Khadij is a Hasan Hadith.

It has been mentioned from Ahmad bin Hanbal that he said: ""The most authentic thing on this topic is the Hadith of Rafi' bin Khadij.""

It has been mentioned from Ali bin Abdullah that he said: ""The most authentic thing on this topic is the Hadith of Thawban and Shaddad bin Aws, because Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated both Hadiths - the Hadith of Thawban and the Hadith of Shaddad bin Aws - from Abu Qilabah.""

Some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others disliked cupping for the one who is fasting, to the extent that some of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) would have themselves cupped at night, among them Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari and Ibn Umar. This is what Ibn Al-Mubarak says.

Abu Eisa said: I heard Ishaq bin Manzur saying: Abdur-Rahman bin Mahdi said: ""Whoever has himself cupped while fasting must make up that day.""

Ishaq bin Manzur said: This is also what Ahmad bin Hanbal and Ishaq bin Ibrahim said.

Abu Eisa said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Az-Za'farani informed me, saying: Ash-Shafi'i said: ""It has been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he was cupped while he was fasting, and it has been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: 'The one who performs cupping and the one who has cupping performed on him have both broken their fast.' I do not know either of these two Hadiths to be firmly established. If a man were to avoid cupping while fasting, that would be more preferable to me. But if a fasting person were to have himself cupped, I would not consider that to break his fast.""

Abu Eisa said: This was the view of Ash-Shafi'i in Baghdad. As for in Egypt, he leaned towards the permissibility, and did not see any harm in cupping for the one who is fasting, using as evidence that the Prophet (ﷺ) was cupped during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was in a state of Ihram and fasting."
775,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""the Messenger of Allah was cupped while he was fasting and in Ihram"
776,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet was cupped while he was fasting"
777,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet was cupped somewhere between Makkah and Al-Madinah and he was fasting and in Ihram"
778,"Anas narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Do not perform Wisal"" They said: ""But you perform Wisal O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""I am not like you are"
779,"Abu Bakr Bin Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hashim said:""Aishah and Umm Salamah"
780,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""When one of you is invited to eat then let him respond"
781,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :The Prophet said: ""When one of you is invited (to a meal) and he is fasting"
782,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""A woman may not fast a day - other than in the month of Ramadan - while her husband is present"
783,"Aishah narrated:""I would not make up what was due upon me from Ramadan except in Sha'ban"
784,"Laila narrated from the one who freed her (Umm Amarah) that:The Prophet said: ""When those who are not fasting eat in the presence of the fasting person"
785,"Habib bin Zaid said:""I heard a freed slave of ours called Laila narrated from [his (Habib's) grandmother] Umm Amarah bint Ka'b Al-Ansar"
786,"(Another chain) from Umm Amarah bint Ka'b Al-Ansari:From the Prophet"
787,"Aishah narrated:""We would menstruate during the time of the Messenger of Allah"
788,"Asim bin Laqit bin Sabrah narrated:From his father who said: ""I said. 'O Messenger of Allah! Inform me about Wudu.' So he said: ""Perform Wudu well"
789,"Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever stays with a people"
790,"Abu Hurairah and Aishah narrated:""The Prophet would perform I'tikaf during the last ten (days) of Ramadan until Allah took him"
791,"Aishah narrated:""When the Messenger of Allah wanted to perform I'tikaf"
792,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would Yujawir (stay in I'tikaf) during the last ten (nights) of Ramadan and he said: 'Seek the Night of Al-Qadr during the last ten (nights) of Ramadan"
793,"Zirr said:""I said to Ubayy bin Ka'b: 'O Abu Al-Mundhir! How do you know that it is the night of the twenty-seventh?' He said: 'Rather"
794,"Uyainah bin Abdur-Rahman narrated:""My father narrated to me: 'The Night of Al-Qadr was mentioned in the presence of Abu Bakrah"
795,"Ali narrated:""The Prophet would awaken his family during the last ten (nights) of Ramadan"
796,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would struggle (to perform Salat more) during the last ten (nights) more than he would struggle in the rest of it"
797,"Amir bin Mas'ud narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Fasting during the winter is an easy reward"
798,"Salamah bin Al-Akwa said:""When the following was revealed: 'And for those upon whom it is difficult"
799,"Muhammad bin Ka'b narrated:""I went to Anas bin Malik during Ramadan and he was about to travel. His mount was prepared for him"
800,"(Another chain) from Muhammad bin Ka'b who said:""I went to Anas bin Malik during Ramadan"" and he mentioned a similar narration (as no)"
801,"Al-Hasan bin Ali narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The gift for the fasting person is (fragrant) oil and a censer"
802,"Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Al-Fitr is the day that the people break the fast"
803,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Prophet would perform I'tikaf during the last ten (nights) of Ramadan. One year he did not perform I'tikaf"
804,"Aishah narrated:""When the Messenger of Allah performed I'tikaf"
805,"That was narrated to us by Quraibah :From Al-Laith (a similar narration as no)"
806,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us** — **Muḥammad ibn al-Fuḍayl narrated to us**, from **Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind**, from **al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Jurashī**, from **Jubayr ibn Nufayr**, from **Abū Dharr** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

""We fasted with the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him), and he did not lead us in prayer until seven nights of the month had remained. Then he stood and led us in prayer until one-third of the night had passed. He did not lead us in prayer on the sixth night, but he led us on the fifth night until half of the night had passed. We said to him, 'O Messenger of Allāh, would you not lead us in voluntary prayer for the remainder of this night?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

**'Indeed, whoever stands in prayer with the imām until he departs, it will be recorded for him as having stood in prayer for an entire night.'**

Then he did not lead us in prayer until three nights of the month remained. He led us in prayer on the third night and summoned his family and his wives, and he stood and led us in prayer until we feared missing the *falāḥ*.""

I said to him, ""What is the *falāḥ*?"" He said, ""**The *suḥūr* (pre-dawn meal).**""

---

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith.

The people of knowledge differed regarding the *qiyām* (night prayer) of Ramaḍān. Some of them held the view that one should pray **forty-one rakʿahs**, including the *witr*. This is the position of the people of Madīnah, and this is the established practice among them in Madīnah.

The majority of the people of knowledge are upon what has been narrated from **ʿUmar**, **ʿAlī**, and others among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), which is **twenty rakʿahs**. This is the position of **Sufyān al-Thawrī**, **Ibn al-Mubārak**, and **al-Shāfiʿī**.

Al-Shāfiʿī said: ""And thus I found the people of our land, Makkah, praying twenty rakʿahs.""

**Aḥmad** said: ""Various narrations have been reported regarding this, and I have not made a definitive ruling on it.""

**Isḥāq** said: ""Rather, we choose forty-one rakʿahs, based on what has been narrated from **Ubayy ibn Kaʿb**.""

**Ibn al-Mubārak**, **Aḥmad**, and **Isḥāq** preferred praying **behind the imām** during the month of Ramaḍān. **Al-Shāfiʿī**, however, preferred that a man pray **alone** if he is a reciter (i.e., one who has memorized the Qurʾān).

There are narrations on this topic from **ʿĀʾishah**, **al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr**, and **Ibn ʿAbbās** (may Allāh be pleased with them all)."
807,"Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever provides the food for a fasting person to break his fast with"
808,"Abu Hurairah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would encourage the night prayer in Ramadan without firmly ordering it"
